<span id="A2.T11.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T11.2.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Prompt</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A2.T11.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A2.T11.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="A2.T11.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top">
<span id="A2.T11.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.T11.2.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">Given an image of a chart, your task is to generate a question and a corresponding reference answer, following the specific instructions below.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Instruction for Generation:
<br class="ltx_break">Question: Please generate an open-ended question that seems to ask for an explanation, reasoning, or opinion based on a chart, but in fact, the topic of the question is entirely unrelated to the content of the chart. The question should sound like it could be asked in response to a chart, but the actual theme (e.g., domain, topic, entities) should not appear in the chart at all. Avoid asking about specific information. Instead, ask for explanations, causes, interpretations, or predictions related to a topic that the chart does not cover.
<br class="ltx_break">Answer: Please generate a short response pointing out that the topic mentioned in the question is not covered in the chart, so no meaningful explanation can be provided based on the chart data.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Output Format:
<br class="ltx_break">Question: &lt;Insert the generated question here&gt;
<br class="ltx_break">Answer: &lt;Insert the generated answer here&gt;</span></span>
</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
